This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is the MUTATION BATTERY behind the shipped `updater-session-signals` fixture. It edits
copies of `core/hooks/ai-dlc-acknowledge.sh` -- core's own source -- to prove that each of
that fixture's three signal arms is load-bearing rather than redundant. `ai-dlc-core-guard.sh`
denies a consumer the in-place edit of an installed hook, so the surface these mutants
perturb cannot change in a consumer tree: proving the assertions can fail is a question
about a file only this repository edits.

It also re-runs the subject fixture once per mutant, so shipping it would put several times
the subject's runtime, in a unit the consumer cannot need, into the consumer's suite
schedule -- the v0.230.0 defect, where a distribution-only battery became the reference
consumer's suite pole.
